---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party software (not bundled, installed by you)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Nothing below is part of this repository; you download it yourself and it keeps its own licence.

Node dependencies of bot/ (see bot/package-lock.json): mineflayer (MIT), minecraft-protocol (BSD-3-Clause), mineflayer-pathfinder (MIT),
minecraft-data (MIT; it contains game-derived and community-wiki-derived data under its own terms) and their dependencies, which are
MIT, BSD, ISC, Apache-2.0, 0BSD and CC0 licensed. brain/, mind/, voice/ and report/ have no npm dependencies.

Java build and test dependencies (voice-mod/, map-addon/, downloaded by Gradle at build time): Fabric Loom (MIT), Fabric Loader and
Fabric API (Apache-2.0), BlueMapAPI (MIT), the Simple Voice Chat API (see below), JUnit 5 (EPL-2.0, tests only), Gson (Apache-2.0, tests only).
Builds also download Mojang's official mappings (Microsoft licence: development use only, no redistribution of the mappings).

Minecraft server mods (downloaded from Modrinth by server/fetch-mods.sh, never redistributed here; check each licence on its Modrinth page):
Fabric API (Apache-2.0), Fabric Language Kotlin (Apache-2.0), BlueMap (MIT), ServerReplay (MIT), Skin Restorer (MIT).

Simple Voice Chat (Max Henkel) is ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. It is not part of this repository and may not be redistributed. Download it yourself
from Modrinth. wrenvoice only compiles against its public API (compileOnly) as an addon, the documented extension mechanism
(https://modrepo.de/minecraft/voicechat/api); the API's licence is not published separately. Do not redistribute wrenvoice together with
the Simple Voice Chat jar, and do not build a container image or archive that contains it.

The Fabric loader and the itzg/minecraft-server container image (Apache-2.0, pinned by digest in server/start.sh) fetch the Minecraft
server, which is subject to the Minecraft EULA (https://www.minecraft.net/en-us/eula). You accept it yourself with MINECRAFT_EULA=accept.

Optional voice stack (you install the servers and models yourself; versions pinned in voice/box/requirements-*.txt):
Kokoro-82M TTS and the kokoro / misaki packages (Apache-2.0), sherpa-onnx (Apache-2.0), NVIDIA parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3 (CC-BY-4.0,
attribution: NVIDIA), torch, numpy, soundfile (BSD; soundfile wraps libsndfile, LGPL-2.1), FastAPI (MIT), uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause),
NeMo toolkit (Apache-2.0).
IMPORTANT: Kokoro's English phonemiser (misaki[en]) installs espeak-ng (GPL-3.0) through espeakng-loader. Installing it yourself in your own
venv is fine; if you redistribute a bundle, venv or container that includes it, you must comply with the GPL for that component and
Apache-2.0 does not cover it.
Streaming STT model: any sherpa-onnx streaming NeMo-transducer model directory you choose (STTS_MODEL_DIR). No model is named or shipped
here; NVIDIA NeMo models are usually CC-BY-4.0, but check the licence of the exact model you download.
No model files are included.

Language models for the brain are not included and not required: any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works. Check the licence of the model you choose.

Test fixtures: no audio is shipped. The voice end-to-end tests skip unless you generate speech clips yourself (voice/tools/make-fixture.mjs, Kokoro-82M);
report and brain fixtures are synthetic.
